Fresh-eyes review complete on `src/blog/people/drafts/Michael-Jordan.md`. The review block is appended at the bottom of the file (no body edits made), written against both the draft and the entity-gap packet.

The two biggest issues flagged:

1. **The 1998–2024 hole.** A table titled "grievance ledger, 1978 to 2026" jumps from 2009 straight to 2024. Missing: the Wizards comeback and the 2003 firing by Abe Pollin — the one grievance in his life that was *real and documented*, which would sharpen the ledger's own point that truth was never the input — and the entire ownership era, including the 7-59 Bobcats, the worst season in NBA history. That's the thesis's hardest test (what does the machine do when the scoreboard turns on him and he can't play?), and the draft skips it.
2. **The Crying Jordan meme is absent from the Hall of Fame section.** The draft describes the tears and even plays the smaller "took that personally" meme earlier, but never says those HOF tears became the internet's most durable humiliation artifact. One sentence closes the loop; its absence reads as a miss, not restraint.

Also flagged: the 1982 UNC shot was in the research file but dropped from the draft ("Mike Jordan became Michael Jordan" is a gift for this thesis), the 2020 George Floyd statement is needed so "Republicans buy sneakers" doesn't read as cherry-picked, and a few trims — the "long, long time" quote appears verbatim twice, and the free throw gets pre-spent in two mid-article references before its payoff ending. The review also marks what to protect: the disambiguation opening, the ledger's middle column, the Bird "praise has no shelf" paragraph, and the final two sentences.
